UGHE Test Web App
===================

Public repositories
-------------------
Backend (Django):  https://github.com/Pacifique5/UGHE-Backend
Frontend (Next.js): https://github.com/Pacifique5/UGHE-Frontend

This file is included in both repositories and is the setup record for the
UGHE Test Web App. The page follows the UGHE homepage at https://ughe.org/
and the supplied screenshot. Every visible item (logo, buttons, menus,
slideshow frames, applications band, Facts & Stats, academics columns,
news stories, impact band, footer, numbers, descriptions, and colours) is
stored in PostgreSQL and edited in Django admin. The Next.js app only
renders the API response.


What was built
--------------
- A Django REST API and Django admin for homepage content.
- A Next.js frontend that renders that content.
- Token login with one predefined staff account.
- A slideshow that accepts one or many images, a YouTube link, or a direct
  video file (.mp4, .webm, .ogg).
- The rest of the landing page from ughe.org: applications, a count-up
  Facts & Stats row, the academics and admissions band, a news carousel,
  the impact band, and the footer. Numbers animate from 0 when the row
  scrolls into view. Bands fade upward. Those timings and colours are
  fields, so they can be changed in Django admin.
- Search over the content already loaded for the page.


Stack and approach
------------------
- Frontend: Next.js (App Router) and TypeScript.
- Backend: Django 5.2 and Django REST Framework.
- Database: PostgreSQL. The role is `postgres` with no password. The
  application database is named `ughe`, so the project tables are not mixed
  into the default `postgres` database.
- Day-to-day development on this machine does not start Docker, because
  Docker can freeze the PC. The same app is still packaged for evaluation:
  each repository has a Dockerfile and a docker-compose.yml. Clone the two
  repositories as sibling folders named backend and frontend, then from
  either folder run `docker compose up --build`. That starts PostgreSQL,
  applies migrations, loads the homepage, and serves Next.js on port 3000.
  The browser calls the API at http://localhost:8000. Inside the frontend
  container, server-side requests use http://backend:8000.
- Libraries are listed in backend/requirements.txt and frontend/package.json.


Font
----
The brief asks for Museo Slab. UGHE publishes that face from its homepage
stylesheet, so the page loads those files first and keeps Roboto Slab as
the fallback the brief allows.

- Name used: Museo Slab
- Found at: https://ughe.org/wp-content/uploads/elementor/css/post-2136.css
  which points at the .ttf files under /wp-content/uploads/2026/04/
- Included in code: frontend/src/app/globals.css declares @font-face for
  Museo Slab and lists it first on the body.
- Fallback name: Roboto Slab
- Fallback found at: https://fonts.google.com/specimen/Roboto+Slab
- Fallback included in code: frontend/src/app/layout.tsx loads it with
  next/font/google (Roboto_Slab). That sets the CSS variable
  --font-roboto-slab. globals.css uses it after Museo Slab, then Rockwell
  and Courier New. Both files contain a comment that records this choice.


Predefined staff account
------------------------
Username: ughe_admin
Password: UGHE-admin-2026

The same account signs in at http://localhost:3000/login and at
http://127.0.0.1:8000/admin/


Folder layout
-------------
backend/                         Django project (UGHE-Backend repository)
  manage.py
  requirements.txt
  ughe_backend/                  settings, root URLs, WSGI
  accounts/                      login, logout, and current-user API
  content/                       models, admin, homepage API, seed command
    management/commands/seed_homepage.py
    seed_data.py                 starting copy taken from the screenshot
  media/                         uploaded and seeded files (created locally)

frontend/                        Next.js project (UGHE-Frontend repository)
  src/app/                       routes: / and /login
  src/components/                header, slideshow, facts, login form
  src/lib/                       API client and shared types


1. PostgreSQL
-------------
Install PostgreSQL and make sure the service is running.
Create the database once (the role `postgres` has no password on this setup):

    psql -U postgres -h localhost -c "CREATE DATABASE ughe;"

If that database already exists, the command reports an error and you can
continue. Connection defaults, all overridable with environment variables
or a backend/.env file copied from backend/.env.example:

    POSTGRES_DB=ughe
    POSTGRES_USER=postgres
    POSTGRES_PASSWORD=
    POSTGRES_HOST=localhost
    POSTGRES_PORT=5432


2. Backend
----------
From the backend directory:

    python -m venv .venv

Windows PowerShell:

    .\.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m pip install -r requirements.txt
    .\.venv\Scripts\python.exe manage.py migrate
    .\.venv\Scripts\python.exe manage.py seed_homepage
    .\.venv\Scripts\python.exe manage.py runserver

macOS or Linux:

    source .venv/bin/activate
    pip install -r requirements.txt
    python manage.py migrate
    python manage.py seed_homepage
    python manage.py runserver

seed_homepage loads the screenshot content, downloads the UGHE logo and
slide images into media/, and creates the staff account. Run it again any
time you want to restore that starting content.

API:
    GET  http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/homepage/
    POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/auth/login/
         JSON body: {"username": "ughe_admin", "password": "UGHE-admin-2026"}
    POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/auth/logout/
         Header: Authorization: Token <token>
    GET  http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/auth/me/
         Header: Authorization: Token <token>

Django admin: http://127.0.0.1:8000/admin/


3. Frontend
-----------
From the frontend directory, in a second terminal:

    npm install
    npm run dev

Optional: copy frontend/.env.example to frontend/.env.local if the API is
not on http://127.0.0.1:8000. The code uses that address when the variable
is unset.

Open http://localhost:3000


4. How to change what the page shows
------------------------------------
1. Open http://localhost:3000/login and sign in, or go straight to Django admin.
2. Edit Site settings, Action links, Navigation items, Hero slides, or
   Page sections (the stats are edited on the section).
3. For a slide, choose Image or Video.
   - Image: upload a file or paste an image URL.
   - Video: paste a YouTube link or a direct video-file URL, or upload a file.
   - An uploaded file is shown instead of the external URL.
4. Uncheck "Is active" to hide an item without deleting it.
5. Refresh http://localhost:3000. The homepage request is not cached.

The first seeded slide uses the Butaro Dialogues caption from the screenshot.
Further slides are included so the slideshow can show more than one image
and a video. Deactivate the extra slides in admin if you want a single frame.


5. Checks
---------
From the backend directory, with the virtualenv Python:

    .\.venv\Scripts\python.exe manage.py test

The tests cover the homepage payload, hidden slides, the predefined login,
a rejected password, and logout.


6. Colours
----------
Stat and button colours are fields on each record. The stat row uses the
live homepage values #C42127 and #8F1A1D. Header buttons stay #E6D4D8 and
the slideshow button stays #79B9BC. The footer is #C22226. Change any of
them in admin and the frontend follows. Count-up duration is also a field:
the first three stats run for 2000ms and 4TH runs for 100ms, matching the
data-counter values on ughe.org.


7. Continuous integration
-------------------------
GitHub Actions runs on every push to main and on every pull request.

Backend workflow: .github/workflows/ci.yml
    - Starts PostgreSQL
    - Installs requirements.txt
    - Runs python manage.py test
    - Media downloads are skipped in CI with SKIP_MEDIA_DOWNLOAD=1 so the
      suite does not depend on ughe.org being reachable. The external URLs
      remain in the database.

Frontend workflow: .github/workflows/ci.yml
    - npm ci
    - npm run typecheck
    - npm run build

The badges on each repository README show the latest result.
